{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493679-goratrix-mirror-have-you-used-it-as-a-plot-hook-how-would-you-use-it","id":1493679,"title":"Goratrix mirror - Have you used it as a plot hook? How would you use it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-25T14:46:42-07:00","id":1493679,"title":"Goratrix mirror - Have you used it as a plot hook? How would you use it?","content":"Im planning to use goratrix mirror (well, kinda) and wanted to see how others have used this plot hook, or how you think it could be used.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have not yet. But my initial idea is that they will find an abandoned underwater chantry used to study the path of neptune. Inside it they will find a mirror with goratrix inside.<br /> <br /> But it's not the real goratrix mirror, Tremere wouldn't let it lying around anyware. My justification is that goratrix, who has a long history of fucking over his childes actually had centuries prior confined one of them to a mirror. Since they have a direct blood relation goratrix managed to subdue the childe soul to &quot;stream&quot; himself into the other mirror, which wasnt much useful until someone discovered this abandoned underwater chantry...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He is still powerless, but he lure the PCs to get this secondary mirror to the surface in exchange for knowledge, maybe even thaumathurgy. But to do it the PCs must first overcome the lovecraftian phenomenon responsible for killing every vampire in the chantry and making it abandoned.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 09-25-2022, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T18:00:31-07:00","id":1493693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493679-goratrix-mirror-have-you-used-it-as-a-plot-hook-how-would-you-use-it#post1493679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im planning to use goratrix mirror (well, kinda) and wanted to see how others have used this plot hook, or how you think it could be used.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have not yet. But my initial idea is that they will find an abandoned underwater chantry used to study the path of neptune. Inside it they will find a mirror with goratrix inside.<br /> <br /> But it's not the real goratrix mirror, Tremere wouldn't let it lying around anyware. My justification is that goratrix, who has a long history of fucking over his childes actually had centuries prior confined one of them to a mirror. Since they have a direct blood relation goratrix managed to subdue the childe soul to &quot;stream&quot; himself into the other mirror, which wasnt much useful until someone discovered this abandoned underwater chantry...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, do you have any particular use for that supposed childe or is that just part of an explanation for the &quot;backup mirror&quot; existence?<br /> <br /> Because if the second, you can just go with that - Goratrix once made one, two or even <i>a whole series</i> of <i>interconnected</i> magic mirrors, each one part of some obscure abandoned magical experiment and related to the peculiar geomancy of a certain chantry dedicated to the studies of a particular path, many of them lost, hidden or outright forgotten due to the vagaries of fate through the ages, or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-25-2022, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T17:59:12-07:00","id":1494066,"title":"","content":"I would have it in the hands of the SI - and debriefing it part of how they have made so many inroads, including the destruction of the Vienna Chantry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T18:18:15-07:00","id":1494071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493679-goratrix-mirror-have-you-used-it-as-a-plot-hook-how-would-you-use-it?p=1494066#post1494066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have it in the hands of the SI - and debriefing it part of how they have made so many inroads, including the destruction of the Vienna Chantry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> This is a very interesting idea. Althought I still think it fits much more that it was Karl schrekt who arranged for the fall of vienna.<br /> <br /> The dude basically said that if he COULD he would destroy the white worm they call tremere. He was a witch hunter in life, and the way he did act as justicar, creating division E and keep working as if he was still a justicar after being dismissed makes me think he totally driven by a strong sense of what is allowed to exist or not.<br /> <br /> Not to mention after all the higher ups died it was HIM who became leader of the pyramid.<br /> <br /> He has the means, he has the reasons. We just don't have a glove yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I guess both can be true. Maybe Karl found goratrix mirror, and with it managed to learn how to bypass the protective rituals that are above his generation and expertise. Or maybe he found the mirror and allowed it to be found by the SI, this way not connecting himself with the SI directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T16:34:51-07:00","id":1509906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493679-goratrix-mirror-have-you-used-it-as-a-plot-hook-how-would-you-use-it?p=1493693#post1493693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, do you have any particular use for that supposed childe or is that just part of an explanation for the &quot;backup mirror&quot; existence?<br /> <br /> Because if the second, you can just go with that - Goratrix once made one, two or even <i>a whole series</i> of <i>interconnected</i> magic mirrors, each one part of some obscure abandoned magical experiment and related to the peculiar geomancy of a certain chantry dedicated to the studies of a particular path, many of them lost, hidden or outright forgotten due to the vagaries of fate through the ages, or something similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to write the same thing! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Since Goratrix was last seen underneath Mexico City in the late 90's, network of interconnected, geomancy-fueled mirros is a pretty neat idea. Goratrix is trapped anyway until someone finds one of those mirrors, fights off the defences, figures out what it is and how to use it. You could build an entire chronicle around this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27765-euderos","name":"Euderos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27765_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T17:55:02-07:00","id":1509911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Euderos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493679-goratrix-mirror-have-you-used-it-as-a-plot-hook-how-would-you-use-it?p=1509906#post1509906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wanted to write the same thing! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Since Goratrix was last seen underneath Mexico City in the late 90's, network of interconnected, geomancy-fueled mirros is a pretty neat idea. Goratrix is trapped anyway until someone finds one of those mirrors, fights off the defences, figures out what it is and how to use it. You could build an entire chronicle around this.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong on that, since it was a storyline jumpstarted by my <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/House_Verditius\" target=\"_blank\">Verditius</a> character in the last Ars Magica game i played, a bunch of years ago. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}